from jsonb_to_recordset($q$[{"position":1,"type":"multi","text":"Based on the Bayes' Theorem application for a standard deck of 52 cards, what is the posterior probability that a randomly drawn card is a King, given that it is a Face card?","options":["1/2","33.33%","1/6","1/3","0.25","75%"],"answer":[1,3],"weight":1,"extra":{}},{"position":2,"type":"multi","text":"In Bayes' Theorem, how is the conditional probability of event A, given that event B has already occurred, formally denoted?","options":["P(B)","P(A|B)","P(A)","P(B|A)"],"answer":[1],"weight":1,"extra":{}},{"position":3,"type":"radio","text":"The linearity of expectation states that the expected value of the sum of random variables is equal to the sum of their individual expected values, but this rule only applies if the variables are independent.","options":["True","False"],"answer":[1],"weight":1,"extra":{}},{"position":4,"type":"radio","text":"If two random variables, X and Y, are known to be dependent on one another, you cannot find the expected value of their sum simply by adding E[X] and E[Y].","options":["True","False"],"answer":[1],"weight":1,"extra":{}},{"position":5,"type":"radio","text":"Bayes' Theorem establishes the relationship between two events exclusively by computing their different conditional probabilities.","options":["True","False"],"answer":[1],"weight":1,"extra":{}},{"position":6,"type":"multi","text":"Which formula is used to compute the Expected Value for categorical variables?","options":["E(n) = n × p","E(x) = n × p","E(x) = nx","E(x) = n × q"],"answer":[1],"weight":1,"extra":{}},{"position":7,"type":"radio","text":"According to the generalized theorem for the linearity of expectation, if a random variable X is multiplied by a constant c, its expected value is also multiplied by that same constant.","options":["True","False"],"answer":[0],"weight":1,"extra":{}},{"position":8,"type":"radio","text":"In the Bayes' Theorem example regarding a standard deck of cards, the probability of initially drawing a King (1/13) acts as the prior probability, while the calculated P(King|Face) acts as the posterior probability.","options":["True","False"],"answer":[0],"weight":1,"extra":{}},{"position":9,"type":"text","text":"In a game where two six-sided dice are rolled, what is the expected value of the sum of the results?","options":null,"answer":"7","weight":1,"extra":{}},{"position":10,"type":"radio","text":"To compute the expected value of the sum of 5 dice throws, you must first calculate the individual probability of every possible sum (from 5 to 30) before averaging them.","options":["True","False"],"answer":[1],"weight":1,"extra":{}}]$q$::jsonb) as x(position int,type text,text text,options jsonb,answer jsonb,weight int,extra jsonb);

